# `get width() { return this.inner.width; }`: the getter itself makes its class the only layout in sight that answers `width`, so by the name alone `this.inner` was expected to be a Shelf: a test that fails
# at every call, a call of the getter by itself on the side that never runs, and the read by name behind a rare edge. Where each name used off a value is answered by the very getter that is being walked, the
# names say nothing.
# RUN: walk f3 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: ShapeTest
# CHECK: PropGet {{*}} key="width"
